; ── 3.5 mm TRS to stereo RCA adapter ───────────────────────────────────────────
;
; A rigid black block, no cord: its 3.5 mm stereo plug goes straight into a 3.5 mm
; jack (a PHONES, a line out, the speakers' line in), the left (white) and right (red) phono jacks sit on its far end. Like
; RfModulator, it is a CompositeCable of ONE plug, PlugA0, which IS the block: no
; PlugB0 and no VerletRope.
;
; ── The frame ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; PlugA0's frame is the model's, RetroXR's plug frame: the origin on the block's
; front face, where a jack's collar stops it; the shaft along +Z into the jack,
; the block and the jacks behind it along -Z, the studded face +Y. Its jacks' mouths
; are the model's RcaJackL (+5.3 mm X) and RcaJackR (-5.3 mm X), 27.7 mm back.
;
; Each jack's zone is its MOUTH, where a seated phono plug's origin belongs, turned
; R_x(180) so the mouth faces PlugA0 -Z (the RF modulator's RF OUT, the same way).
; show_jack is off: the model draws its own shells and insulators.
[node name="TrsRcaAdapter" type="Node3D"]
script = ExtResource("1_script")
cord_colors = PackedColorArray(0.094, 0.094, 0.102, 1)

